  "description": "This application seeks retrospective planning permission for the retention of a small timber shed located within the front garden of the property. The shed has been erected in order to provide secure and weatherproof storage for household items.\n* The shed is modest in scale and sits below the height of the existing front boundary fence, ensuring it is not visually prominent from the public realm.\n* The shed is constructed from timber of the same material and colour as the boundary fence, creating a unified appearance and preventing visual clutter.\n* The structure is positioned so that it does not impede pedestrian or vehicular access and does not harm neighbouring amenity.",
